{"abstract":"Reading academic literature in digital formats is becoming more and more of a normalcy for students, but designers of reading support tools do not share common, metrics for evaluating such tools. This paper introduces our work in developing an evaluation form which we call the aRSX (active Reading Support IndeX). The aRSX-form is a quantitative means for evaluating whether a specific software or hardware tool supports active, academic reading in a way that resonates with personal user experience and learning preferences-in other words; whether the tool is practical and pleasant to use for the student who consumes academic literature. The paper presents the first and second iterations of the aRSX evaluation survey based on a preliminary exploratory experiment with 50 university students. The paper also describes how the evaluation form can be developed and used by designers of reading support tools.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Barkhuus, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381811"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Academic reading","Digital reading","Reading support tools","User experience evaluation","aRSX evaluation form"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"developing evaluation metrics for active reading support","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86106752/CSEDU_aRSX.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381811","identifier":[{"id":"85136984735","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2407420d-8136-4e85-95c9-23edf33d8c1a"],"keyword":["Academic reading","Digital reading","Reading support tools","User experience evaluation","aRSX evaluation form"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-376990C54B027E0F139793C4F7A88E6C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.scitepress.org/Papers/2021/104067/104067.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86106752/CSEDU_aRSX.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5220/0010406701770188","eisbn":["9789897585029"],"pages":"177-188","publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th International Conference on Computer Supported Education (CSEDU 2021)","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136984735"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2407420d-8136-4e85-95c9-23edf33d8c1a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Developing Evaluation Metrics for Active Reading Support","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381811","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Academic reading, a form of active reading, often involves interaction with the text. Highlighting and annotating are some of the most common strategies of interacting with academic texts, yet we have limited understanding of exactly how such interactions affect reading comprehension in digital versus analog reading environments. In this paper, we present an exploratory study, comparing how university students (n = 50) interact with a digital and a physical text, focusing on highlights and annotations. We compare reading time, interaction with, and subsequent memory of the texts. We make nine observations about reading time, highlighting and annotation frequency and memory scores between paper and laptop. We find that students annotate significantly less on laptop than on paper, but that neither highlighting nor annotations influence subsequent memory of the text in either condition. Our broader contribution is to augment understanding of how different interaction features aid academic reading in a natural environment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Barkhuus, Louise","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384207"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Academic reading","Active reading support","Digital reading","Text annotation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interacting with academic readings a comparison of paper and laptop","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86600745/1_s2.0_S2590291121001224_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384207","identifier":[{"id":"85136957631","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c8877010-89b2-41dd-8f9f-b07f03b2724e"],"keyword":["Academic reading","Active reading support","Digital reading","Text annotation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67BB47A184955140C2A61F8369D2C963"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86600745/1_s2.0_S2590291121001224_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["25902911"],"journal":"Social Sciences & Humanities Open","paperid":"100226","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Social Sciences & Humanities Open"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136957631"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c8877010-89b2-41dd-8f9f-b07f03b2724e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interacting with academic readings — A comparison of paper and laptop","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384207","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The design of wearable, tangible and embedded interactive products requires a focus on bodily/kinesthetic aspects of the user experience, that is, how the product \"feels\" in use. Although best practice in user-centered design (such as iterative design, prototyping, user testing) also applies for this new type of product, the designer's skill set needs to be supplemented with design methods and practices that utilize bodily intelligence and empathy with the user. We present a framework for categorizing such body-centered design practices based on two dimensions: point-of-view (1st, 2nd, 3rd person) and tense (past, present, future). Inspired by Merleau-Ponty's phenomenology of the body, Shusterman's work on somaesthetics, and Buber's theories on intersubjectivity, the framework provides a language for talking about different ways designers and co-designers can utilize their body as a design resource. The intention is not to be prescriptive on method, but to provide guidance during planning, execution and analysis.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Svanæs, Dag","Barkhuus, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382103"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bodily Intelligence","Co Design Practices","Phenomenology","User Centered Design","Wearable Computing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the designer s body as resource in design exploring combinations of point of view and tense","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85551140/Svanaes_Barkhuus_Open.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382103","identifier":[{"id":"85091299408","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-38d439d2-5319-4983-8142-ffa29ca63673"],"keyword":["Bodily Intelligence","Co-Design Practices","Phenomenology","User-Centered Design","Wearable Computing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-969CC38D583C79A445A9685F5817FB42"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85551140/Svanaes_Barkhuus_Open.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"svanæspau","last":"Svanæs","name":"Svanæs, Dag","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3313831.3376430","eisbn":["9781450367080"],"pages":"1-13","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"CHI '20: Proceedings of the 2020 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091299408"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-38d439d2-5319-4983-8142-ffa29ca63673"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Designer’s Body as Resource in Design: Exploring Combinations of Point-of-view and Tense","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382103","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Watching television together in the living room is a joyful and social activity that most people can relate to. As a result of the ongoing COVID19 outbreak, many friends and family members are separated due to national lockdowns and quarantine. In this demo we show how a web application can support real-time socially based video-content by facilitating a virtual living room for friends and family where they can watch synchronized video content while interacting. Our prototype uses readily available web-technologies, allowing users to get started in just one click by logging in with their existing YouTube account. Data from the YouTube API are then fed into novel recommender algorithms that then suggest videos based on the user’s collective interests. Info available at https://beta.letswatch.net","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bryld, Jannik Munk","Schønrock, Lucas","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Barkhuus, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383472"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Recommender algorithms","Synchronized video content","Virtual living room","Web based social interaction","YouTube API"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"watching together but apart shared video experiences during covid 000000000019 outbreak","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.c.5020919.v3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383472","ids":["itu-964c92a3-58c7-4aee-adcb-268ef3ebe8c1"],"keyword":["Recommender algorithms","Synchronized video content","Virtual living room","Web-based social interaction","YouTube API"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-938F10934A026D85369215F5369FB323"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://figshare.com/articles/conference_contribution/Demo7_-_Bryld_Sch_nrock_L_vlie_Barkhuus/12496727","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85386004/Bryld_Sch_nrock_L_vlie_Barkhuus_IMX.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.c.5020919.v3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannik Munk","key":"bryldpau","last":"Bryld","name":"Bryld, Jannik Munk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lucas","key":"schønrockpau","last":"Schønrock","name":"Schønrock, Lucas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.6084/m9.figshare.c.5020919.v3","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Adjunct Proceedings of the ACM International Conference on Interactive Media Experiences (IMX) 2020"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-964c92a3-58c7-4aee-adcb-268ef3ebe8c1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Watching Together but Apart: Shared Video Experiences During COVID-19 Outbreak","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383472","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
