{"abstract":"The transition into motherhood is a complicated and often unsupported major life disruption. To alleviate mental health issues and to support identity re-negotiation, mothers are increasingly turning to online mothers’ groups, particularly private and secret Facebook groups; these can provide a complex system of social, emotional, and practical support for new mothers. In this paper we present findings from an exploratory interview study of how new mothers create, find, use, and participate in ICTs, specifically online mothers’ groups, to combat the lack of formal support systems by developing substitute networks. Utilizing a framework of critical infrastructures, we found that these online substitute networks were created by women, for women, in an effort to fill much needed social, political, and medical gaps that fail to see ‘woman and mother’ as a whole being, rather than simply as a ‘discarded candy wrapper’. Our study contributes to the growing literature on ICT use by mothers for supporting and negotiating new identities, by illustrating how these infrastructures can be re-designed and appropriated in use, for critical utilization.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Britton, Lauren","Barkhuus, Louise","Semaan, Bryan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384897"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ithaca College","Syracuse University"],"keyword":["ICT utilization","Identity re negotiation","Motherhood transition","Online mothers groups","Social support networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mothers as candy wrappers critical infrastructure supporting the transition into motherhood","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84899780/GROUP2020_Camera_Ready_new_Mama.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384897","identifier":[{"id":"85076699304","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f61ccea7-7346-4f8b-8512-c14bfd3a9ee2"],"keyword":["ICT utilization","Identity re-negotiation","Motherhood transition","Online mothers' groups","Social support networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9A8BDB7342BC60C1A5184E7129E6621"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84899780/GROUP2020_Camera_Ready_new_Mama.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"ithaca college","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Ithaca College","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"syracuse university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Syracuse University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lauren","key":"brittonpau","last":"Britton","name":"Britton, Lauren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bryan","key":"semaanpau","last":"Semaan","name":"Semaan, Bryan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3361113","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"GROUP","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076699304"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f61ccea7-7346-4f8b-8512-c14bfd3a9ee2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"\"Mothers as Candy Wrappers\": Critical Infrastructure Supporting the Transition into Motherhood","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384897","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present an interview study of 13 recent newcomers to New York City, focusing on their early experiences of exploration and use of mobile location services and other tools for getting to know their new city. We describe their reasons and intentions behind exploratory practices using digital tools and emphasize how they make meaning out of new places in relation to technology tools as well as their previous places. Mobile location technologies make the process of finding specific places and exploring new neighborhoods a digital search task but discourage the notion of wandering and exploration. We point out missed opportunities for socio-technical systems supporting place making and place discovery and suggest that digital exploration tools should stay peripheral to the activities that people enjoy as tech-free but support a wider notion of search for salient characteristics of places.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Barkhuus, Louise","Wohn, Yvette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384274"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","New Jersey Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Location based services","Mobile technologies","place technologies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"making the city my own uses and practices of mobile location technologies for exploration of a new city","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00779-018-01191-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384274","identifier":[{"id":"85057978301","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-cd353e84-9efc-4409-a06a-285260b19872"],"keyword":["Location based services","mobile technologies","place technologies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D84424971022CB7C9682F7337A025742"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00779-018-01191-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84065470/PUC03_1019_final_proof.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"new jersey institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New Jersey Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yvette","key":"wohnpau","last":"Wohn","name":"Wohn, Yvette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00779-018-01191-z","issn":["16174909","16174917"],"issn_org":["16174909"],"journal":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing","pages":"1-10","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057978301"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-cd353e84-9efc-4409-a06a-285260b19872"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Making the city my own: uses and practices of mobile location technologies for exploration of a new city","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384274","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a case study of a fully working prototype of the Sensus smart guitar. Eleven professional guitar players were interviewed after a prototype test session. The smartness of the guitar was perceived as enabling the integration of a range of equipment into a single device, and the proactive exploration of novel expressions. The results draw attention to the musicians’ sense-making of the smart qualities, and to the perceived impact on their artistic practices. The themes highlight how smartness was experienced in relation to the guitar’s agency and the skills it requires, the tension between explicit (eg playing a string) and implicit (eg keeping rhythm) body movements, and to performing and producing music. Understanding this felt sense of smartness is relevant to how contemporary HCI research conceptualizes mundane artefacts enhanced with smart technologies, and to how such discourse can inform related design issues.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rossitto, Chiara","Rostami, Asreen","Tholander, Jakob","McMillan, Donald","Barkhuus, Louise","Fischione, Carlo","Turchet, Luca"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384804"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Queen Mary University of London","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Artistic practice","Human Computer Interaction HCI","Musicians Sense Making","Smart Guitar","Smart Technologies in Music"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"musicians initial encounters with a smart guitar","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84047135/p13_rossitto.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384804","identifier":[{"id":"85056577350","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f01bbea4-00b4-40e3-91cf-d88d7dad46f2"],"keyword":["Artistic Practice","Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)","Musicians’ Sense-Making","Smart Guitar","Smart Technologies in Music"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78CCEFF4B18B1FAB1EE705786EA2871F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://mcmillan.it/papers/p13-rossitto.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84047135/p13_rossitto.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chiara","key":"rossittopau","last":"Rossitto","name":"Rossitto, Chiara","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asreen","key":"rostamipau","last":"Rostami","name":"Rostami, Asreen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob","key":"tholanderpau","last":"Tholander","name":"Tholander, Jakob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Donald","key":"mcmillanpau","last":"McMillan","name":"McMillan, Donald","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlo","key":"fischionepau","last":"Fischione","name":"Fischione, Carlo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"turchetpau","last":"Turchet","name":"Turchet, Luca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3240167.3240223","isbn":["9781450364379"],"pages":"13-24","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '18 Proceedings of the 10th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056577350"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f01bbea4-00b4-40e3-91cf-d88d7dad46f2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Musicians’ Initial Encounters with a Smart Guitar","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384804","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This workshop invites the CSCW community to explore hybrid events-large collocated events where technology is used to support audience participation. We argue that the technology landscape has changed since the early studies in CSCW towards this context. Therefore, the research foci must similarly change and focus on studying the practices or propose alternative and novel interfaces. This workshop helps the CSCW community to consider the research agenda for the next generation of hybrid event studies. We do this by discussing the open conceptual, empirical and constructive research problems in this domain. Together with the organizers and participants, we seek to develop a research agenda and seek opportunities for further collaboration on the topic of hybrid events.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nelimarkka, Matti","Jacucci, Giulio","Salovaara, Antti","Dow, Steven","O'Hara, Kenton","Barkhuus, Louise","Fisher, Joel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383173"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","title":"ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["Aalto University","All Global Affiliations","University of Bristol","University of California","University of Helsinki","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Audience Participation","CSCW","Hybrid Events","Research agenda","Technology Integration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid events mediating collocated participation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84065476/p455_nelimarkka.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383173","identifier":[{"id":"85058130945","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-81b14ee7-b803-4152-902c-81be7f9d4990"],"keyword":["Audience Participation","CSCW","Hybrid Events","Research Agenda","Technology Integration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99785372EAA156E1E123CAFC9DA67972"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84065476/p455_nelimarkka.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fi","key":"aalto university","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aalto University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fi","key":"university of helsinki","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Helsinki","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of bristol","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bristol","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matti","key":"nelimarkkapau","last":"Nelimarkka","name":"Nelimarkka, Matti","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresp