{"abstract":"New parents are faced with the challenge of quickly acquiring a new base of knowledge, while simultaneously navigating a significant life change. While both new mothers and fathers experience new and unique parental demands, their early caregiving challenges differ and new mothers often search for different types of support and information online. We here present findings from an exploratory interview study of how new first-time mothers navigate online resources as they transition into parenthood. We find that many parenting tasks are supported by a variety of resources, which are often used in combination to accomplish a task. We also found that variety in sources was often valued over general source credibility, and new mothers relied on their own ability to filter information to assess how much to trust information. We also provide more general insight into the methods individuals used to gain domain knowledge in a completely new area.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Barkhuus, Louise","Bales, Elizabeth","Cowan, Lisa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381803"],"event":{"acronym":"HICSS","title":"Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of California"],"keyword":["Early caregiving challenges","Information filtering","Knowledge acquisition","New parents","Online resources"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"internet ecologies of new mothers trust variety and strategies for managing diverse information sources","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24251/HICSS.2017.276","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381803","identifier":[{"id":"85108220981","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-23b14062-9d30-45d7-bc19-4b3cb6ee4b75"],"keyword":["Early caregiving challenges","Information filtering","Knowledge acquisition","New parents","Online resources"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-873FC169CB315EC8B69C0A5F88F3AA46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.24251/HICSS.2017.276","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82932913/paper0282.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Elizabeth","key":"balespau","last":"Bales","name":"Bales, Elizabeth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisa","key":"cowanpau","last":"Cowan","name":"Cowan, Lisa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.24251/hicss.2017.276","isbn":["9780998133102"],"pages":"2283-2292","publisher":"University of Hawai'i at Manoa","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 50th Hawaii International Conference on System Sciences"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108220981"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-23b14062-9d30-45d7-bc19-4b3cb6ee4b75"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Internet Ecologies of New Mothers: Trust, Variety and Strategies for Managing Diverse Information Sources","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381803","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a case study of an interactive performance that was produced and designed to encourage civic engagement and reflection in relation to the social tensions in a low-income suburb, mostly inhabited by people with immigrant backgrounds. The technological setup in the performance encouraged participation by means of text entries that audience members could share with others. The analysis draws on the corpus of interview and observational data collected, as well as the related text messages that were shared during the performance. We illustrate the different levels at which citizens make sense of societal issues they are concerned about, as well as the audience-citizens’ perception of participating in such an artistic experience","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rossitto, Chiara","Normark, Maria","Barkhuus, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384998"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm University","Södertörn University"],"keyword":["Audience Participation","Civic engagement","Immigrant Backgrounds","Interactive Performance","Social Tensions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interactive performance as a means of civic dialogue","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82933021/rossito_chi2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384998","identifier":[{"id":"85044855411","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fe32770e-fc00-4f0d-beac-98dcf0f17eea"],"keyword":["Audience Participation","Civic Engagement","Immigrant Backgrounds","Interactive Performance","Social Tensions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0363EA284F542D607A75F7730BDFDEED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82933021/rossito_chi2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"södertörn university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Södertörn University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chiara","key":"rossittopau","last":"Rossitto","name":"Rossitto, Chiara","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"normarkpau","last":"Normark","name":"Normark, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3025453.3025897","eisbn":["9781450346559"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044855411"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fe32770e-fc00-4f0d-beac-98dcf0f17eea"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Interactive Performance as a Means of Civic Dialogue","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384998","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In recent years, several mobile applications allowed individuals to anonymously share information with friends and contacts, without any persistent identity marker. The functions of these “tie-based” anonymity services may be notably different than other social media services. We use semi-structured interviews to qualitatively examine motivations, practices and perceptions in two tie-based anonymity apps: Secret (now defunct, in the US) and Mimi (in China). Among the findings, we show that: (1) while users are more comfortable in selfdisclosure, they still have specific practices and strategies to avoid or allow identification; (2) attempts for de-identification of others are prevalent and often elaborate; and (3) participants come to expect both negativity and support in response to posts. Our findings highlight unique opportunities and potential benefits for tie-based anonymity apps, including serving disclosure needs and social probing. Still, challenges for making such applications successful, for example the prevalence of negativity and bullying, are substantial.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ma, Xiao","Andabili, Nazanin","Barkhuus, Louise","Naaman, Mor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382736"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","Drexel University"],"keyword":["De identification","Self disclosure","Social media","Tie based anonymity","User behavior"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"people are either too fake or too real opportunities and challenges in tie based anonymity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82932981/ma_chi2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382736","identifier":[{"id":"85044863179","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6225b9c3-1bb9-4bd6-9d0b-9819626b3be7"],"keyword":["De-identification","Self-disclosure","Social media","Tie-based anonymity","User behavior"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2C065ABFC1BA8B7F1DA757B336739323"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82932981/ma_chi2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"drexel university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Drexel University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiao","key":"mapau","last":"Ma","name":"Ma, Xiao","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nazanin","key":"andabilipau","last":"Andabili","name":"Andabili, Nazanin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mor","key":"naamanpau","last":"Naaman","name":"Naaman, Mor","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3025453.3025956","eisbn":["9781450346559"],"pages":"1781-1793","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044863179"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6225b9c3-1bb9-4bd6-9d0b-9819626b3be7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"\"People Are Either Too Fake or Too Real\": Opportunities and Challenges in Tie-Based Anonymity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382736","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Digital technologies provide theater with new possibilities for combining traditional stage-based performances with interactive artifacts, for streaming remote parallel performances and for other device facilitated audience interaction. Compared to traditional theater, mixed-media performances require a different type of engagement from the actors and rehearsing is challenging, as it can be impossible to rehearse with all the functional technology and interaction. Here, we report experiences from a case study of two mixed-media performances; we studied the rehearsal practices of two actors who were performing in two different plays. We describe how the actors practiced presence during rehearsal in a play where they would be geographically remote, and we describe the challenges of rehearsing with several remote and interactive elements. Our study informs the broader aims of interactive and mixed media performances through addressing critical factors of implementing technology into rehearsal practices.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Barkhuus, Louise","Rossitto, Chiara"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382269"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","end":"2016-05-12","place":"San Jose, us","start":"2016-05-07","title":"ACM CHI 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Digital technologies","Interactive Artifacts","Mixed media performances","Rehearsal practices","Remote performance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acting with technology rehearsing for mixed media live performances","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85015100398","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382269","identifier":[{"id":"85015100398","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-438192eb-9d38-458e-989b-5ba6c555c41a"],"keyword":["Digital technologies","Interactive artifacts","Mixed-media performances","Rehearsal practices","Remote performance"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-875FDC3927AC714E5A28A8AB33080CB8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Chiara","key":"rossittopau","last":"Rossitto","name":"Rossitto, Chiara","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2858036.2858344","isbn":["9781450333627"],"pages":"864-875","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM Annual Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","status":"p","subtitle":"CHI '16","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-438192eb-9d38-458e-989b-5ba6c555c41a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Acting with Technology: Rehearsing for Mixed-Media Live Performances","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382269","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"A core aspect of collaboration tools is the sharing of awareness cues, such as availability and location information, often with the purpose of more efficient collaboration and communication between individuals. In this paper, we present a user study of a continuous location-sharing application, used for a month within groups of 4-5 people, which provided a detailed awareness between group members. Reporting on issues such as its facility for micro-coordination and enabler of ad-hoc social engagements, we analyze the distinct ways in which the service was incorporated into participants’ daily lives. We studied a location sharing service among people in less hierarchical types of relationships than previous studies and found that sharing concerns were based in the participants ‘thinking’ and imagination of potential situations rather than in actual situations. Our findings highlight how people’s understanding of location-tracking technologies is transitional and how it includes a constant re-negotiation of appropriate services and applications for everyday social management. We conclude that map-based continuous location sharing has significant utility among tight-knit dyads.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schildt, Emily","Leinfors, Martin","Barkhuus, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381248"],"event":{"acronym":"GROUP","title":"ACM International Conference on Supporting Group Work"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Ad Hoc Social Engagements","Awareness Cues","Collaboration Tools","Location Sharing","Micro coordination"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"communication coordination and awareness around continuous location sharing","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85006024462","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381248","identifier":[{"id":"85006024462","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0004c4d6-f1e4-4817-a15a-2dd6bbe9799d"],"keyword":["Ad-Hoc Social Engagements","Awareness Cues","Collaboration Tools","Location Sharing","Micro-Coordination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88DBE3503A2337CCEC77AE3CE3F93C9F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emily","key":"schildtpau","last":"Schildt","name":"Schildt, Emily","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"leinforspau","last":"Leinfors","name":"Leinfors, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2957276.2957289","isbn":["9781450342766"],"pages":"257-265","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"GROUP '16 Proceedings of the 19th International Conference on Supporting Group Work"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006024462"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0004c4d6-f1e4-4817-a15a-2dd6bbe9799d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Communication, Coordination and Awareness around Continuous Location Sharing","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381248","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Mobile social matching systems aim to bring people together in the physical world by recommending people nearby to each other. Going beyond simple similarity and proximity matching mechanisms, we explore a proposed framework of relational, social and personal context as predictors of match opportunities to map out the design space of opportunistic social matching systems. We contribute insights gained from a study combining Experience Sampling Method (ESM) with 85 students of a U.S. university and interviews with 15 of these participants. A generalized linear mixed model analysis (n=1704) showed that personal context (mood and busyness) as well as sociability of others nearby are the strongest predictors of contextual match interest. Participant interviews suggest operationalizing relational context using social network rarity and discoverable rarity, and incorporating skill level and learning/teaching needs for activity partnering. Based on these findings we propose passive context-awareness for opportunistic social matching.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mayer, Julia","Barkhuus, Louise","Hiltz, Starr Roxanne","Vaananen, Kaisa","Jones, Quentin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381693"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","New Jersey Institute of Technology","Tampere University of Technology"],"keyword":["Experience sampling method","Mobile Social Matching Systems","Opportunistic Social Matching","Personal Context","Relational Context"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"supporting opportunities for context aware social matching an experience sampling study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85014741876","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381693","identifier":[{"id":"85014741876","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1c9f3b6e-b7a4-471e-b532-693c70b41c2f"],"keyword":["Experience Sampling Method","Mobile Social Matching Systems","Opportunistic Social Matching","Personal Context","Relational Context"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6F77A1E5D6BD8F8E2267BF574B814731"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"new jersey institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New Jersey Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"tampere university of technology","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Tampere University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julia","key":"mayerpau","last":"Mayer","name":"Mayer, Julia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","locid":"831421c0-027f-4a25-b795-ee2fce0c8d2a","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-1306-249X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Starr Roxanne","key":"hiltzpau","last":"Hiltz","name":"Hiltz, Starr Roxanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kaisa","key":"vaananenpau","last":"Vaananen","name":"Vaananen, Kaisa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Quentin","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","name":"Jones, Quentin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2858036.2858175","isbn":["9781450333627"],"pages":"2430-2441","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM Annual Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1c9f3b6e-b7a4-471e-b532-693c70b41c2f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Supporting Opportunities for Context-Aware Social Matching: An Experience Sampling Study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381693","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"HCI research has explored mobile technologies to support social activity and to support greater feelings of connected- ness. Much of this has focused on different mobile devices, individual preferences and modes of use. Yet social activity and connectedness are about ongoing enactments of relationships across technologies. We propose the relational lens as a way to include a notion of relational tension in addition to individual preferences in the design and analysis of mobile communication technologies. We discuss three strategies people use to manage tensions in their relationships: selection, segmentation and integration. Our data show that use of social technologies can at times destabilize social relations and occasion relational tensions, forcing users to renegotiate how they enact these relationships.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Shklovski, Irina","Barkhuus, Louise","Bornø, Nis","Kaye, Joseph 'Jofish'"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383507"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","end":"2015-03-18","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2015-03-14","title":"The 18th ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm University","Yahoo Labs"],"keyword":["Friendship","Information sharing","Mobile communication","Social network sites","personal relationships"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"friendship maintenance in the digital age applying a relational lens to online social interaction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84968761501","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383507","identifier":[{"id":"84968761501","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9852f71e-78e2-4e0c-a959-094cf4fee3af"],"keyword":["friendship","information sharing","mobile communication","personal relationships","social network sites"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-8F8E6C8470EEF3E334D9C655FF7BE496"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"yahoo labs","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yahoo Labs","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"shklovskipau","last":"Shklovski","name":"Shklovski, Irina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nis","key":"bornøpau","last":"Bornø","name":"Bornø, Nis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Joseph 'Jofish'","key":"kayepau","last":"Kaye","name":"Kaye, Joseph 'Jofish'","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781450329224"],"pages":"1477-1487","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM Conference on Computer-Supported Cooperative Work and Social Computing","status":"p","title":"CSCW '15 Proceedings of the 18th ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work &amp; Social Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84968761501"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9852f71e-78e2-4e0c-a959-094cf4fee3af"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Friendship maintenance in the digital age: Applying a relational lens to online social interaction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383507","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"HCI research has explored mobile technologies to support social activity and to support greater feelings of connectedness. Much of this has focused on different mobile devices, individual preferences and modes of use. Yet social activity and connectedness are about ongoing enactments of relationships across technologies. We propose the relational lens as a way to include a notion of relational tension in addition to individual preferences in the design and analysis of mobile communication technologies. We discuss three strategies people use to manage tensions in their relationships: selection, segmentation and integration. Our data show that use of social technologies can at times destabilize social relations and occasion relational tensions, forcing users to renegotiate how they enact these relationships.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Shklovski, Irina","Barkhuus, Louise","Bornoe, Nis","Kaye, Joseph 'Jofish'"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-693037"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","end":"2015-03-18","place":"Vancouver, ca","start":"2015-03-14","title":"18th ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work &amp; Social Computing (CSCW '15)","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stockholm University","Yahoo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"friendship maintenance in the digital age applying a relational lens to online social interaction","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/record/display.uri?eid=2-s2.0-84968761501&origin=inward&txGid=0","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-693037","identifier":[{"id":"84968761501","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d0916bc6-7ffa-4d41-82e3-786fc4ebe85c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-8F8E6C8470EEF3E334D9C655FF7BE496"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Information Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Research Centre for Socio-Interactive Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"yahoo","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Yahoo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"shklovskipau","last":"Shklovski","name":"Shklovski, Irina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nis","key":"bornoepau","last":"Bornoe","locid":"5d796fd0-3